# Finding 1 (RESULTS.md), a new candidate: the stream s loses s29, which its publisher confirm
# acknowledged, for good after rabbit3's power loss while rabbit1 is away. rabbit2 is killed
# before step 1 and back before step 4; rabbit1 is paused from step 16 to step 27 (about 100 s,
# past the net tick time); rabbit3 loses its power before step 21 and starts again before step
# 24. A stream confirms a chunk once a majority of its members wrote it, and never syncs
# (osiris, as documented). Epoch 2's writer rabbit3 and its replica rabbit2 confirmed s29, and
# rabbit3's copy was in its page cache. After the power loss the stream coordinator elected
# rabbit1 from the quorum rabbit1 and rabbit3, while rabbit2's replica waited on a retry timer.
# rabbit2 then deleted its whole log, s29 with it, and copied the log again from rabbit1. The
# window is narrow: on this image the run passes without any one of its faults; N= and G= (a bit
# of a classic queue's transient store, which the workload does not use) move the moment of the
# confirm. On e2's image K=, P= and L= alone were enough. Found blind by `hydo explore` (e2's
# seed 2).
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none dseed=0 | run K=rabbit2@1+3 N=nodes.bridge.6@21-23:loss,100% P=rabbit1@16+11 W=5764a73c,p3,q2,r1000 G=rabbit3@20:flip,n=4,seed=4979bdc4 L=rabbit3@21+3
